1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kicked a pebble,
and even my shoe flew off.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,240
Goofing around,
right on the head of the gym teacher,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed, saying I was
still as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,140
Somewhere, a bit of good spirit,

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
even as a sound, it hits hard,
so there's proof of it.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
a nightmare,
the streetscape that never changes,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler, somehow.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,880
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,920
the sun is already setting.

11
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:53,880
Are there really yakitori stalls?

12
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,740
retired from people.

14
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:04,060
The sun is sinking.

15
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,060
Tomorrow too, it ends with dropping things

16
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,720
Published in a magazine,
happiness again, they say.

17
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,660
I only realized it after losing it.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,320
Because I'm such a fool.

19
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,720
Granny,
what are you doing in a place like this?

20
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:38,860
How to handle the knife

21
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,540
The way you shape the rice

22
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,560
Speed

23
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:44,520
No matter which one you pick,

24
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,600
they hold up well against anyone.

25
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,100
About Kankichi

26
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:51,120
I've made up my mind.

27
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,820
Choukanda Sushi

28
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,440
The noren-wake showdown

29
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,480
What did you say?

30
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:09,260
Kankichi, don't suddenly shout like that!

31
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,420
Sorry about that.

32
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:16,660
Your skill as a sushi chef has
reached the level of the very best.

33
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,360
Why don't you try running your own shop?

34
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,760
I said don't shout!

35
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,120
So, which shop is it?

36
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:32,820
It's a shop inside the Sky Tower that Mr.
Nakagawa's company just completed this month.

37
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:37,720
The world's tallest skyscraper that's
having its grand opening next month?

38
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:43,820
At Mr. Nakagawa's request, we've been
chosen to open a branch there as a tenant.

39
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:50,300
Wow, I can't believe I'll
get to have my own shop!

40
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:54,400
The rights to the shop
will all be mine, right?

41
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,520
You promise that too, right?

42
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,320
Here are the specifics.

43
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,740
There are conditions from their side.

44
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:01,840
What is it?

45
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:08,060
The condition is that Nakagawa Suisan Shoji
handles all the supply of fish for the shop.

46
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,840
Every seafood item gets an IC tag.

47
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,178
Place of origin, freshness, price,

48
00:03:13,228 --> 00:03:17,160
and quality are all managed
responsibly by Nakagawa Suisan,

49
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:20,620
so it's apparently a system where
people can eat sushi with peace of mind.

50
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:24,560
So it's high-tech sushi, then.

51
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:27,260
That kind of thing is
Kankichi's specialty, right?

52
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:30,360
It's not a branch,
it's an independent shop with its own noren.

53
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,560
Do your best.

54
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:35,940
Even if you get the shop, you won't
have a single yen in operating funds.

55
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:37,780
We'll lend you 10 million
yen with no collateral.

56
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,420
You pay it back within three years.

57
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:42,600
Yay! Just as expected of Gepard!

58
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,620
I'll make it a shop to my own taste!

59
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:48,460
Grandma,
are you sure about leaving it to Kankichi?

60
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:51,500
Don't worry,
he has a talent for making money.

61
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:55,500
But if it's for profit,
he might cut corners on quality.

62
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:58,500
That's fine,
there are IC tags to take care of that.

63
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:01,940
I can't wait, it's my shop!

64
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,520
Manager

65
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:10,180
What's with that shocked look?

66
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,500
Do you two find it a
nuisance having me as manager?

67
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,840
No, not really.

68
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:19,400
But that shop is important
to the Nakagawa Group too,

69
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:23,480
Nakagawa! What's wrong with me
running that important shop?!

70
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:24,559
Ry-

71
00:04:24,609 --> 00:04:28,980
We're worried you'll lower the quality to make money,
Ryo-chan.

72
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:32,232
Gepard and Matei said the same thing.

73
00:04:32,282 --> 00:04:34,840
Why doesn't anyone trust me?

74
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:39,980
They even said they wanted to implant
an IC tag in me to track my movements.

75
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:43,740
Ah what a good idea. Let's do that.

76
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:47,380
But Ryo-chan, what about the police?

77
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,380
Of course.

78
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,100
You're quitting?!

79
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,020
Obviously.

80
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:55,823
From now on, the best sushi shop in Japan,

81
00:04:55,873 --> 00:04:59,340
no, the best in the world.
That's what I'm aiming for.

82
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:02,380
You two had better come and eat there too!

83
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,400
I'm home.

84
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:11,640
Big bro.

85
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,360
Long time no see, Matoi.

86
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:15,120
What's come over you all of a sudden?

87
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:19,260
Rejoice, Matoi! I've returned
after finishing my training in Kyoto.

88
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:21,780
Please hold Yu-tsu and Mikan too.

89
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,500
Come on, Mikan, come here.

90
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:26,320
Up, up!

91
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:30,960
So that means we can live together
again after all these years.

92
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,760
Now we can play catch again.

93
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:37,520
Grandma, since big bro has come home,

94
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:41,780
shouldn't the Sky Tower branch be
handed to big bro rather than Kankichi?

95
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:48,400
We were just discussing that together.

96
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:53,400
As far as we're concerned, if he can
do it well, nothing could be better.

97
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:57,180
But we already told
Kankichi he'd be in charge.

98
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:01,680
Oh right, that idiot went and
submitted his resignation, didn't he?

99
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:07,020
Lemon's also gotten an email
asking us to give advice.

100
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,820
It can't be helped. Here,

101
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:13,260
What?

102
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:18,000
This isn't what we agreed on!

103
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:21,380
We've already put everything on the table!

104
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,480
Hear me out to the end.

105
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:26,240
I never said I wouldn't leave it to you.

106
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:30,880
So that's why Super
Kanda Sushi can't go ahead.

107
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:34,100
We want to take the best
possible course of action too.

108
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:35,940
Let's make it two shops.

109
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:37,920
Two shops?

110
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,540
We're just splitting the shop in two.

111
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:49,780
The grand opening is next month. Until then, we'll hold a one-week trial opening,
and whichever of you two makes more profit will get to run the shop.

112
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:51,760
I don't mind.

113
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:52,640
As for Kankichi,

114
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:58,640
It's not a matter of whether we do it or not!
My whole future is on the line here. You already accepted it, didn't you!

115
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:03,660
I trained in Kyoto, and I'll fight
fair and square with my skills.

116
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,740
Big brother, I'll help you too.

117
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:33,340
We advertised with flyers beforehand,
so there's a line of customers.

118
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:35,080
Everyone's really fired up.

119
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:37,080
How's Kankichi's side doing?

120
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:45,940
Can Kankichi really manage
with just the two of them?

121
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:48,980
Since supplies are
controlled by Nakagawa Suisan.

122
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:53,420
We can't go under.
We have no choice but to cut labor costs.

123
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:57,160
I see. But from what I can see,
they look like amateurs.

124
00:07:57,400 --> 00:08:01,170
Yeah, that's right. They made me
take a whole week off out of nowhere,

125
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:05,200
and on top of that, I'm only getting 1,000 yen a day.
Awful, isn't it?

126
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,810
Don't say unnecessary things.

127
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:11,260
I told you that if I won, I'd let you
eat sushi for the rest of your life.

128
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,640
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

129
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,620
Welcome!

130
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,380
Today, as a grand opening special,

131
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,300
top-grade nigiri sushi flyer

132
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:31,440
we're serving them both for just 500 yen.

133
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,080
That cheap?

134
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:35,820
From across the street?

135
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,100
500 yen?

136
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:42,020
That's half our price, bro!

137
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:43,600
No need to panic.

138
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,400
At 500 yen with this quality of topping,
there's barely any profit.

139
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,300
Let's just keep doing what we're doing.

140
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,300
Here you go, one top-grade chirashi bowl!

141
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,900
And one top-grade chirashi over here,

142
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:54,380
Coming right up!

143
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:57,480
I'm just going to the bathroom,
you're in charge.

144
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,800
Yes, I'll take it.

145
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,960
Kohada and amberjack, got it.

146
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,940
For me, this one, sayori.

147
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:03,140
Coming right up!

148
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:05,020
How about some kohada?

149
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:09,400
Atari-mo-hakke, anyone?

150
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:12,020
Here you are, sorry to keep you waiting.

151
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:12,820
Thank you.

152
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,160
Hey, isn't the rice ball a bit big?

153
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,440
It's on the house.

154
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,520
What is this!

155
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:25,500
Idiot! We're not making picnic lunches here!

156
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:27,780
Sorry for the wait, here's your order.

157
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,900
Hey! Here's your kohada, sorry for the wait!

158
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:34,680
Sure, it's skillful,
but I haven't washed my hands.

159
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:37,980
Don't worry, after I've made two or three more,
my hands will be clean.

160
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:41,217
It's a foreigner.

161
00:09:41,267 --> 00:09:44,920
I'm really bad at English, you know.

162
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,140
Is this a sushi bar?

163
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,960
Doesn't matter what,
a customer is a customer.

164
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,260
Go figure something out.

165
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:52,680
Just a moment, please.

166
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,100
What's going on?

167
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:03,860
Because I don't understand English at all.

168
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,360
It seems they went to the shop next door.

169
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:06,560
I see.

170
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:10,060
With our location,
we have to win over foreign customers too.

171
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:12,680
Is this a sushi bar?

172
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,080
So it's a foreigner.

173
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,960
Big brother, my English is...

174
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:17,735
Don't make me do it.

175
00:10:17,785 --> 00:10:21,660
Foreign tourists also flocked to
the ryotei restaurants in Kyoto.

176
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,575
Yes! Sushi bar,

177
00:10:23,625 --> 00:10:26,280
sushi bar, right! Please sit down!

178
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,840
Please, please! Japanese tea, right!

179
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,960
What? You're saying the profit is the same?

180
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:38,670
Sales of the citrus ones
are overwhelmingly higher, but

181
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,680
the profit was small, after all.

182
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:47,320
Because all the foreign customers
went over to the Yūutsu shop.

183
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:54,420
Now master everything by tomorrow!
No way, senpai, that's impossible!

184
00:10:55,320 --> 00:11:00,580
I'm going to come up with sushi
that satisfies foreign customers too!

185
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:12,160
We made this menu for foreign
customers all night last night.

186
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:16,020
With this, they can just point
at the pictures and understand.

187
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:16,660
Yeah.

188
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,240
Good afternoon!

189
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:23,840
Please, please!

190
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:28,360
Welcome! This way, please!

191
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:30,600
What country are they from, do you think?

192
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,380
Probably Indian.

193
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:35,280
Is there even sushi
that suits Indian people?

194
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,500
Don't worry!
I prepared something for that properly!

195
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:43,360
Here you go!
Curry sushi made with dry curry!

196
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:51,500
Very, very good!

197
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,080
We did it!

198
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,800
Oh, so it's light

199
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:59,360
I don't get it at all.

200
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:03,440
Don't worry, he says he wants
the light bonito as an appetizer.

201
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,740
So tataki, then.

202
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:08,880
No, let's go with bonito carpaccio,
Italian style.

203
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:10,960
You can make that?

204
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:14,180
No problem, I've made it before in Kyoto.

205
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:15,240
Here you go, one order up!

206
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,020
Ooh, it's delicious.

207
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,600
What? They say we're losing a little?

208
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:40,180
In sales, we're completely winning, though.

209
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:44,320
Sure, they get more customers,
but their ingredient costs are double.

210
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:47,800
Kankichi's place makes far
too many dishes in advance.

211
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:52,240
If it comes to this,
I'll make the shop more striking.

212
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:56,920
Matoi, our shop has plenty of customers too,
but no repeat customers at all.

213
00:12:56,920 --> 00:13:00,280
Yes, they're all first-time customers.

214
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,440
So they only come because it's novel?

215
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:05,400
Yes, before long the customers will dry up.

216
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:08,200
We need a calm shop that
makes people want to come back.

217
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:12,000
Right, let's go back to basics, Wada.
Let's push a Japanese atmosphere.

218
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:13,640
So that's how you'll play it.

219
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,860
Maybe I'll do it in a kimono.

220
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:17,300
Yeah, let's do that.

221
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:24,740
Really, what a noisy man he is.

222
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:37,000
Ikehara, nice,
a considerate touch befitting a woman.

223
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,900
Grand reopening!

224
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,860
Kankichi, what are you planning?

225
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,320
It's a trade secret.

226
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:53,140
Alright, it's noon.
From today, let's treasure a calm harmony.

227
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:56,180
Whoa, what is this?

228
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,440
What's this commotion?

229
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:03,580
Please don't push, don't push.
Buy your balls first, then play.

230
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:10,320
How can you call this a sushi shop?

231
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,820
Take it easy.

232
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:14,820
Yes, I got the opening one!

233
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:16,180
Congratulations.

234
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:17,980
One fatty tuna!

235
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:19,540
Yes! Sea urchin!

236
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,180
We've got sea urchin over here too!

237
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:22,840
Hey! Congratulations, aye!

238
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:24,520
I owe you again.

239
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:26,240
I want to eat some tuna.

240
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,340
Hurry up and finish!

241
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,360
The people behind us are
getting tired of waiting!

242
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,260
How's the Pachi-sushi?

243
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:34,040
A customer with good
taste can fill their stomach

244
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,340
for just 100 yen.

245
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:38,240
Well, there aren't many
customers like that, though.

246
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,640
Sounds just like Kankichi, though.

247
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:42,020
Can you do something about this noisy music?

248
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:43,700
Alright, alright.

249
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,700
Still, what a crowd this is.

250
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:49,040
Hey, the fatty tuna isn't coming out!

251
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:51,420
Coming right up!

252
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,620
Sea urchin, sea urchin!

253
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:55,800
Amberjack and sea urchin!

254
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,700
Tuna, prime fatty tuna, nonstop!

255
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:00,980
Hey, congratulations, you!

256
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:02,620
Senpai!

257
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:07,400
Look, we're out of
fatty tuna and sea urchin!

258
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,760
What, it's all gone already?

259
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:13,420
Everyone at this counter ate it all!

260
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,640
W-who's the one selling here?

261
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,100
Still no sea urchin or negitoro!

262
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:23,320
Wait, isn't that the pachinko
pro from the pachinko magazine!

263
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:24,980
Hurry up!

264
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,660
Y-yes, sir, coming right up!

265
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:36,120
Nyaa! We've run out of toppings and rice!

266
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:43,780
Free gift of extra balls!
I'll be back tomorrow too!

267
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:47,800
Senpai, if they keep coming tomorrow too,
we'll be in the red big time!

268
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:49,620
Forget the Bachi sushi.

269
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:55,080
Orders for the people who are waiting.

270
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:00,840
He's trying to start something again.

271
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:02,720
Edomai Sushi Get Racing!

272
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:05,400
Rules: pull out the sushi you want to eat.

273
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:09,320
Alright,
we'll go for the expensive ones first!

274
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:12,440
Oh, we crashed!

275
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,680
Isn't this game over?!

276
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:19,877
Heh,

277
00:16:19,927 --> 00:16:24,290
Even F1 racers would find this course hard,
so I've set the difficulty to five,

278
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,600
You can't pull out the sushi!

279
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:27,040
Mo!

280
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:30,020
Tikke Marty! Sweet shrimp! Gatsu!

281
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:32,100
No way, that's impossible!

282
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:33,040
Alright,

283
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:36,440
Next is Tamago Tou! Amagai Dance! Gatsu!

284
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:39,120
What is that?!

285
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:45,700
Otoro...

286
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:48,120
It's fast!

287
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:52,380
But I'm a pro in this world too!

288
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:54,580
I can't afford to lose!

289
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:59,700
W-wow, what a run!

290
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:02,040
You're really going to pull out the otoro?!

291
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:05,380
What technique! Amazing!

292
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:09,600
Ooh!

293
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:10,280
Ooh!

294
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,780
As expected of the otoro!

295
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,720
Looks like you won't be easy to beat.

296
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,058
But you...

297
00:17:17,108 --> 00:17:20,480
are too confident in the
weight of your toppings.

298
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:23,140
Otoro is too heavy!

299
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:27,020
But my sushi with light
toppings can be pulled out!

300
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:28,100
I won!

301
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:29,840
I won't lose!

302
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:59,260
!

303
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:00,340
Who are you?

304
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:02,320
Thank you for the meal.

305
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,100
Tomorrow too.

306
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:05,340
We'll be back.

307
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,260
An F1 driver's

308
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:08,360
Schumacher.

309
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,000
Hey,

310
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,640
why would the real

311
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,640
F1 driver's

312
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,080
Schumacher come here?

313
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,560
Forget that, too.

314
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,500
Already on the fifth day,

315
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,180
we've fallen quite far behind, haven't we.

316
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:25,240
At this rate,

317
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:26,620
the shop will be

318
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:28,620
left in Yuutsu-san's hands, it seems.

319
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:32,220
No, we still have two more days.

320
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:34,280
We'll definitely surpass them.

321
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:37,460
Senpai, the renovation costs alone

322
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:40,200
have already eaten up the ten
million yen in operating funds.

323
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:44,240
And we only have what
seafood is left in the fridge.

324
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,160
We can't possibly beat Yuutsu-san's shop.

325
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:50,480
If it comes to this, we have no
choice but to use our secret weapon.

326
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,760
Secret weapon?

327
00:18:57,840 --> 00:19:01,220
Senpai, what are you planning to
do by cutting off just the tails?

328
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:04,660
leaving only the tails
with the IC tags attached,

329
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,140
and then sell off the rest.

330
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:09,360
If you do that,
we won't be able to make any sushi!

331
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:12,920
We'll use the money from
the sales to buy cheap fish.

332
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:18,400
What's all the commotion?

333
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:21,360
It's 300 yen?

334
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:24,620
It's even cheaper than
the opening day special!

335
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:27,820
Has Kankichi lost it and gone desperate?

336
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:33,520
With this,
tomorrow we'll hit a game-changing home run!

337
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:42,400
Welcome!

338
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:43,360
Welcome!

339
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:44,940
Welcome!

340
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:46,080
Welcome!

341
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:46,360
Welcome!

342
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,320
Welcome!

343
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:47,620
Welcome!

344
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:48,680
Welcome!

345
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:49,220
Welcome!

346
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:50,080
Welcome!

347
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:50,360
Welcome!

348
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:50,580
Welcome!

349
00:19:56,220 --> 00:19:57,040
That's it.

350
00:19:57,040 --> 00:20:01,660
A man of your caliber should record
today's books and submit them right away.

351
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,740
Grandma, how did it go?

352
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:13,300
Actually, the profits came out to
exactly the same amount on both sides.

353
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,380
W-what, that's absurd!

354
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:21,640
Damn it, if we'd had five more minutes, we would have won,
since that many customers were still there!

355
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:25,320
They can't be running at a loss at 300 yen.
They must be cheating.

356
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:26,700
No way, that's ridiculous.

357
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:31,560
All the fish we use has
Nakagawa Suisan's IC tags on it.

358
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:34,060
Then show us the fish you have left.

359
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:37,260
We've already sold off
all the leftover fish.

360
00:20:38,420 --> 00:20:39,620
What is this tuna?

361
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,660
Isn't this marlin?

362
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,280
Marlin.

363
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:46,820
The tuna we got from Nakagawa
Suisan should be bluefin tuna.

364
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:52,220
Come on, Lemon. You must have a fever today,
and your tongue must be off.

365
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:57,080
That's not true. Kankichi,
bring the bones of the fish you filleted.

366
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:57,700
That's...

367
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,840
Honda-san, please bring them over.

368
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:01,620
Yes.

369
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:08,100
Look, it even has an IC tag attached, see?

370
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:12,580
It's marlin after all.

371
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:13,620
No way!

372
00:21:13,620 --> 00:21:16,180
Kankichi, then what is this?

373
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:18,420
It's sea bream, obviously.

374
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:20,360
But the tail is yellowtail!

375
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:21,500
Gulp!

376
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:23,200
Suspicious. Let me see it.

377
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,680
You glued that on, didn't you?

378
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:30,440
You idiot, I told you again
and again not to make a mistake!

379
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:35,260
Just as I thought.
Looks like the match is over.

380
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,400
You'd better pay back the 10 million yen.

381
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:42,800
After all that hard work we put in...

382
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:47,460
Nakagawa-san and Reiko-san.

383
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:51,700
Good evening. We got curious
about the contest and came over.

384
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,940
What happened to Matoi-chan?

385
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:56,840
Kankichi cheated, so Big Brother won.

386
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:58,560
Congratulations, Yutsu-san.

387
00:21:59,240 --> 00:21:59,600
Thank you very much.

388
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:05,100
Let's all celebrate Yutsu, who's
become just the right new store manager!

389
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:08,140
Kankichi, make some Batsujaa sushi!

390
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:09,460
Yeah, yeah.

391
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,720
Come on, everyone, please keep eating!

392
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:21,260
This is really delicious.

393
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:25,880
Yu-san, with this,
you could easily represent Japan.

394
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:26,660
Thank you very much.

395
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:30,320
Is the Kankichi nigiri
order still not ready?

396
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:32,040
It just came out now.

397
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:33,780
Honda, I'll take it over.

398
00:22:33,780 --> 00:22:34,340
Here you go.

399
00:22:35,300 --> 00:22:36,420
Here's the small dish.

400
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:39,340
Itadakimasu!

401
00:22:41,940 --> 00:22:45,620
Yeah, yeah, yeah, it's delicious!

402
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:48,760
Delicious!

403
00:22:49,340 --> 00:22:51,416
The thickness of the toppings,
the vinegar in the rice,

404
00:22:51,466 --> 00:22:54,200
the shaping of the nigiri,
everything is perfect!

405
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:55,440
What?!

406
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:59,170
It's better than the sushi I made! Well,

407
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:01,880
We lost! Senpai's sushi is really good!

408
00:23:02,060 --> 00:23:04,420
It's really delicious!
Ryo-chan, you're good!

409
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:11,740
Granny, I'm going to Kyoto
again to start my training over.

410
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:13,540
Well then, everyone, take care.

411
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:14,520
Big brother.

412
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:16,720
Yūutsu.

413
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:22,400
He's gone again.

414
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:28,700
Damn, that means we could have
won if we'd just played normally.

415
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:33,240
Wait, if Yūutsu's gone, that means

416
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:35,160
I'll become the store manager.

417
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:43,140
No way! After coming back after years,
you sent Yūutsu back to Kyoto again!

418
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:46,620
Why does it always end up like this?!

419
00:24:37,420 --> 00:24:43,880
Auntie, you should turn that corner too,
come see!

420
00:24:45,180 --> 00:24:49,060
You'll get to meet everyone!

421
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:56,920
That's Kameari over there surely Kameari!

422
00:24:56,920 --> 00:25:02,200
Come on, everyone, to our town!

423
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:06,880
That's Kameari over there!

424
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:10,220
Surely Kameari!

425
00:25:11,700 --> 00:25:15,320
Come on, everyone, to our town!

426
00:25:16,620 --> 00:25:17,020
Thank you!

427
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:22,440
Some bigwig wants to hold a cherry blossom viewing party,
they say.

428
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:25,560
And it's supposedly a legendary
cherry tree that blooms all year round.

429
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:27,520
As if such a thing really exists.

430
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:28,400
Can't be helped.

431
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:31,160
Leave it to me, the Katsushika Hanami Chief!

432
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:37,000
Cherry blossoms, here we come! A Heisei romance,
a storm of cherry blossoms! Nice to meet you!

433
00:25:38,660 --> 00:25:41,180
That's Kameari over there!

434
00:25:41,180 --> 00:25:44,500
Well, surely Kameari!

435
00:25:44,500 --> 00:25:49,120
Come on, everyone, to our town!

436
00:25:50,020 --> 00:25:50,700
Thank you!

